From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LibreScoot <librescoot@example.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: apply the Cortex-A9 MP errata on the DBC's i.MX6DL

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific configuration]

The DBC carries an i.MX6DL: two Cortex-A9 cores, r2p10, no ACP. ARM
errata 751472, 794072, 761320 and 845369 apply to MPCore configurations,
and 845369 ("transition into streaming mode might create a data
corruption") describes cross-core corruption of the kind seen here.

None of them are reachable on this build. 761320, 794072 and 845369 have
no upstream Kconfig symbol at all, and ARM_ERRATA_743622 and
ARM_ERRATA_751472 both depend on !ARCH_MULTIPLATFORM, which an i.MX6
mainline build violates.

The bootloader cannot close the gap on its own: it runs only on CPU0,
and the diagnostic register (CP15 c15, c0, 1) is banked per CPU, so CPU1
comes out of SMP bringup with its reset defaults. __ca9_errata runs in
the per-CPU setup path that secondary cores also traverse, so the bits
are applied here for every core. The values match the ones NXP's U-Boot
sets for a DualLite.

Signed-off-by: LibreScoot <librescoot@example.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm/mm/proc-v7.S
+++ b/arch/arm/mm/proc-v7.S
@@ -374,12 +374,24 @@
 	ALT_UP_B(1f)
 	mrclt	p15, 0, r0, c15, c0, 1		@ read diagnostic register
 	orrlt	r0, r0, #1 << 11		@ set bit #11
 	mcrlt	p15, 0, r0, c15, c0, 1		@ write diagnostic register
 1:
 #endif
+	@ i.MX6DL: the multi-core Cortex-A9 workarounds are unreachable through
+	@ Kconfig here (761320/794072/845369 have no upstream symbol; 743622 and
+	@ 751472 depend on !ARCH_MULTIPLATFORM). U-Boot can only set these on
+	@ CPU0, and the diagnostic register is banked per-CPU, so apply them here
+	@ where secondary cores pass through too.
+	mrc	p15, 0, r0, c15, c0, 1		@ read diagnostic register
+	orr	r0, r0, #1 << 4			@ 794072: set bit #4
+	orr	r0, r0, #1 << 6			@ 743622: set bit #6
+	orr	r0, r0, #1 << 11		@ 751472: set bit #11
+	orr	r0, r0, #1 << 21		@ 761320: set bit #21
+	orr	r0, r0, #1 << 22		@ 845369: set bit #22
+	mcr	p15, 0, r0, c15, c0, 1		@ write diagnostic register
 	b	__errata_finish
 
 __ca15_errata:
 #ifdef CONFIG_ARM_ERRATA_773022
 	cmp	r6, #0x4			@ only present up to r0p4
 	mrcle	p15, 0, r0, c1, c0, 1		@ read aux control register
